  "checks": [
    "Inspected original tar members, exact package inventory, each prebuilt ELF and compiler receipt; compared elaborated source hashes to the ordinary, reviewed and stream-only producer inputs.",
    "Installed and relocated the original archives, verified the selected XS digest, then ran the public example and TAP clients with no compiler on PATH. Both independently built packages were exercised in both orders. Repeated the public checks on an XS-only installation.",
    "Real Future objects on IO::Async deliver all nineteen scalars, typed factory and terminal IO failures, and returned Except data. Separate checks exercise two pending workers, an unrelated timer, cooperative and ignoring cancellation, abandoned futures, fork/thread affinity, false-valued host exception identity, and cancellation inside result conversion.",
    "Lazy stream factory and one pull per demand, exact typed step errors, Unit versus exhaustion, early close, overlapping demand rejection and native retirement. Real interpreter threads clone a live cursor and a cursor with a pending pull; the owner remains usable after thread teardown. Shared runtime initializes once; identities and descriptors return to baseline.",
    "The offline-installed CLI reproduces both ordinary archives and their package-set receipt byte for byte."
